id:                     E2166
trigger_tool:           conan|pkg-config|meson|clang
phase:                  generate|cross-build
error_signature:        fatal error: 'ogg/ogg.h' file not found|opusfile public header includes an invisible libogg provider

severity:               1
category:               conan|pkg-config|transitive-header|provider-contract
match_keywords:         ogg/ogg.h, opusfile.h, libogg, PkgConfigDeps, pkg_config_name, Requires ogg opus, transitive public header
title:                  Expose a transitive public-header provider through the generated pkg-config graph

root_cause:             A dependency graph can contain libogg while the consumer-visible opusfile component still generates only Requires: opus. Because opusfile.h publicly includes ogg/ogg.h, the successful graph and the first header repair do not close the public compile interface. Marking dependency traits transitive did not change the generated module. A direct consumer edge makes libogg visible, and PkgConfigDeps must project its upstream module name as ogg rather than the Conan package name libogg.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 consumers whose generated component pkg-config module exposes a public header that includes a header from a graph-present but consumer-invisible provider.
verification_cmd:       Run the exact generated-contract positive/negative matrix, then a fresh isolated OHOS/armv8 graph info and install --build=never requiring ogg.pc plus Requires: ogg opus; complete current-snapshot target W3 separately.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           direct-public-provider-edge-and-exact-pkgconfig-name
rec_description:        Add the real public-header provider as a direct requirement, set its PkgConfigDeps pkg_config_name to the module consumed by the dependent component, and fail closed unless both the generated provider file and exact Requires sequence exist.
rec_command:            self.requires("libogg/1.3.5"); pkgconfig.set_property("libogg", "pkg_config_name", "ogg"); require ogg.pc and exact Requires: ogg opus
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-consumer-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      provider-recipe-version-fix
fallback_description:   Publish a corrected provider version whose component metadata exposes the public libogg edge and expected module name, then remove the consumer repair after a fresh W0 and W3.
fallback_command:       fix and publish a new opusfile provider recipe version, then re-resolve the downstream graph with --build=never
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          dependency-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       (C|CXX)FLAGS.*ogg|extra_(c|cxx|ld)flags.*ogg
forbid_1_reason:        Global include or link injection hides an incomplete generated provider contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   Unrelated targets inherit flags while pkg-config consumers remain semantically broken.
forbid_2_pattern:       #\s*include\s*[<"](?:\.\./)*ogg\.h[>"]|#\s*(?:if|ifdef|ifndef|elif).*OHOS
forbid_2_reason:        Patching the upstream public include or adding a platform-name branch avoids rather than fixes provider propagation.
forbid_2_consequence:   Other consumers keep receiving an invalid public interface and portability regresses.

principles:             P005,P010
causes:                 []
caused_by:              [E6409]
similar_to:             [E321,E327]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

